7 Model III: Impact of National Characteristics on
Cybercrime
   This model aims to use advanced modeling methods to conduct an in-depth
analysis of how national characteristics (such as economic level, education level, and
legal strength) influence cybercrime rates and their interactions with the Five
Elements (Metal, Wood, Water, Fire, Earth).



