1. The Rising Cybersecurity Challenge




                                                    型
Cybercrime is a global security and economic threat, with projected $10.5 trillion USD in
damages by 2025. Nations with weak laws, poor data governance, and outdated
cybersecurity policies are at higher risk. Without data-driven, adaptive policies,




                                                  模
ransomware, financial fraud, and cyber espionage will continue to escalate.




                                                学
2. The Five-Element Cybersecurity Framework

